        "math_academy_id": "q-165244",
        "problem": "Given the curve $r(t)=\u27e8\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{t}^{2},\\,t\u27e9,$ use the cross product curvature formula to find the curvature of this curve as a function of $t.$ \n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that* ${r}^{\u2032}(t)\\times {r}^{\u2033}(t)=-\\sqrt{2}\\,i+2t\\,j-\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}\\,k.$",
        "worked_solution": "The curvature $\u03ba(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\u03ba(t)=\\frac{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\\times {r}^{\u2033}(t)\u2016}{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t){\u2016}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and $\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}t,\\,1\u27e9 \\\\ \u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{({t}^{2})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2}t)}^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${t}^{2}+1>0$ for any real value $t.$\n\nSince we are told that\n\n$$\n{r}^{\u2032}(t)\\times {r}^{\u2033}(t)=-\\sqrt{2}\\,i+2t\\,j-\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}\\,k,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\\times {r}^{\u2033}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{(-\\sqrt{2})}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+4{t}^{2}+2{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03ba(t) & =\\frac{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\\times {r}^{\u2033}(t)\u2016}{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t){\u2016}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1)}{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
